Source:
module math

add(a: Int, b: Int {
  a + b
}

---
error: module name does not match its file
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:1:8
  │
1 │ module math
  │        ──┬─
  │          ╰─ this declares module `math`
  ╰─

`src/main.pooka` must declare `module main`.

note: A module is named after its file, without `.pooka`.

error: missing `)`
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:3:4
  │
3 │ add(a: Int, b: Int {
  │    ───────┬───────
  │           ╰─ parameter list is not closed
  ╰─

Expected `)` before `{`.

Found 2 errors.

